  "trial_outcome": "success",
  "reasoning": "This trial tested whether pre-emptive skin treatment could reduce EGFR inhibitor-associated skin toxicities compared to reactive treatment. The primary endpoint (percentage with grade 2+ skin toxicities) was met, showing 29% vs 62% incidence (33% absolute reduction). This is a supportive care intervention trial rather than a direct test of anti-cancer efficacy. The pre-emptive approach successfully reduced skin toxicities while maintaining similar anti-cancer activity (ORR 15% vs 11%). Both arms received identical panitumumab + irinotecan + FOLFIRI regimens, differing only in skin toxicity management strategy.",
